+/* chimera: 0 while the frontend is fast-forwarding. The TIA's picture is a
+ * write-only side product - the priority chain in renderPixel only READS object state,
+ * and the collision latches the 6507 can see are updated in updateCollision(),
+ * not here - so a frame nobody is going to look at can skip all of it. The
+ * frame-layout detector is the one reader that is not a person: it decides
+ * NTSC or PAL from the colours it sees, and that IS the machine, so it is
+ * served whatever the frontend asked for. */
+extern "C" int chimera_render_enabled;
+
